    summary: "Ethiopia is facing renewed fighting in the north, just four years after the devastating Tigray war ended.",
    preview: "Ethiopia is facing renewed fighting in the north, just four years after the devastating Tigray war ended. With tensions rising with Eritrea and wider regional rivalries involving Egypt and Sudan, could this conflict spread beyond Ethiopia’s borders? Al Jazeera’s Lina-Serene explains.",
